<file path="docs/commands/debug.mdx">
---
title: Debug Command
---

### Contains several commands that can help with testing or debugging.

`/exposure debug expose_rgb` - makes 3 B&W exposures with **red**, **green** and **blue** filters. Uses camera settings if player holds a [Camera](../content/camera) in hand.\
`/exposure debug chromatic_from_last_three_exposures` - creates an exposure using chromatic process (combining rgb channels into one image). Uses last 3 exposures from history of the executing player, that are not chromatics themselves.\
`/exposure debug develop_film_in_hand [keep_original]` - develops a [Film](../content/attachments/film) in player's hand.\
`/exposure debug clear_rendering_cache` - Clears cached images. Probably only be useful to me.
</file>

<file path="docs/commands/export.mdx">
---
title: Export Command
---

### Exports exposures as PNG files to `<instance>/exposures` folder on client's PC.

<div name='NOTE' style={{ display: 'inline-block', margin: '2px' }}>
    <div style={{ display: 'flex', alignItems: 'top', backgroundColor: '#232425', borderRadius: '6px', padding: '8px 12px' }}>
      <RocketIcon style={{ color: '#F4EFE9', marginRight: '8px' }} width={20} />
      <span style={{ color: '#F4EFE9', fontSize: '15px' }}>Exported files will be organized in folder with world name, unless turned off in a config.</span>
    </div>
</div><br/>

`/exposure export id <id> <size> <look>` - exports single exposure.\
`/exposure export all <size> <look>` - exports all exposures of the current world. Asks for confirmation.\
`/exposure export stop` - stops export that is currently in progress.

`<size>` - size modifier of exported image. Exporting 320px (default) exposure with size x2 will produce 640px png.\
`<look>` - style of the exposure. Exported file will be suffixed with it so you can export multiple looks without them overriding each other.
</file>

<file path="docs/commands/palette.mdx">
---
title: Palette Command
---

`/exposure palette export` - Exports palette as png or json file.\
`/exposure palette convert` - Converts between png and json. Converted file would be placed in the same folder. Can be used to create palette from image.
</file>

<file path="docs/commands/shader.mdx">
---
title: Shader Command
---

### Allows applying vanilla shaders (post effects) for testing purposes or just for fun.

`/shader apply <player> <shaderLocation>` - applies specified shader (the ones used in filters and others). Available shaders will be shown as autocomplete suggestions.\
`/shader remove <player>` - cancels applied shader effect.
</file>

<file path="docs/commands/show.mdx">
---
title: Show Exposure Command
---

`/exposure show id|texture|latest [negative]` - Shows exposures as photographs.\
`latest` will show a recent history of exposures made by you or another player, if specified.
</file>

