<file path="docs/content/attachments/film.mdx">
---
title: Film
id: exposure:color_film
type: item
---

Film rolls are inserted into a [Camera](../camera) and store your exposures. Single roll can store up to **16** frames.

<Asset location="exposure:black_and_white_film" width={50}/> **Black and White Film**\
<Asset location="exposure:color_film" width={50}/> **Color Film**\
<Asset location="exposure:high_sensitivity_black_and_white_film" width={50}/> **High-Sensitivity Black and White Film**\
<Asset location="exposure:high_sensitivity_color_film" width={50}/> **High-Sensitivity Color Film**
<div style={{ display: 'inline-block', margin: '2px' }}>
    <div style={{ display: 'flex', alignItems: 'top', backgroundColor: '#232425', borderRadius: '6px', padding: '8px 12px' }}>
      <RocketIcon style={{ color: '#F4EFE9', marginRight: '8px' }} width={20} />
      <span style={{ color: '#F4EFE9', fontSize: '15px' }}>*High-Sensitivity film rolls are brighter but have noise*</span>
    </div>
</div><br/>

## Renaming
You can quickly rename the film by ***using*** the item.\
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;• Renaming this way does not cost experience and can be of a great help to identify/organize rolls.\
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;• Renamed rolls keep their new name when developed.

## Developing
<Asset location="exposure:developed_black_and_white_film" width={50}/>**Developed Black and White Film**\
<Asset location="exposure:developed_color_film" width={50}/>**Developed Color Film**

When you are finished with the roll, you need to develop it to make it suitable for printing in [Lightroom](../lightroom).

<Asset location="exposure:black_and_white_film" width={50}/> **Black and White Films** are developed by crafting the roll with just a single **Water Bottle**.\
<Asset location="exposure:color_film" width={50}/> **Color Films** are developed by crafting the roll with **Awkward Potion**, **Thick Potion** and **Mundane Potion**.

<br/>

<div style={{ display: 'inline-block', margin: '2px' }}>
    <div style={{ display: 'flex', alignItems: 'top', backgroundColor: '#232425', borderRadius: '6px', padding: '8px 12px' }}>
      <RocketIcon style={{ color: '#F4EFE9', marginRight: '8px' }} width={20} />
      <span style={{ color: '#F4EFE9', fontSize: '15px' }}>Film does not store actual images, but **information** about the shot you took. This is not a real world after all.</span>
    </div>
</div><br/>

<div style={{ display: 'inline-block', margin: '2px' }}>
    <div style={{ display: 'flex', alignItems: 'top', backgroundColor: '#21252b', borderRadius: '6px', padding: '8px 12px' }}>
      <InfoIcon style={{ color: '#63b3eb', marginRight: '8px' }} width={20} />
      <span style={{ color: '#63b3eb', fontSize: '15px' }}>You can customize several properties of the Film: [Custom Films](../../customization/custom_films)</span>
    </div>
